1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,930
I've known that guy for a long time.

2
00:00:02,380 --> 00:00:04,210
He really loves
beef stew.

3
00:00:06,460 --> 00:00:08,760
(Why did I even make
beef stew?)

4
00:00:08,760 --> 00:00:11,300
(And why did I expect Haru senpai to show up?)

5
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:17,270
Hey, Minato!

6
00:00:17,270 --> 00:00:19,190
The audition date is set!

7
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:20,230
Audition?

8
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:21,600
Yeah.

9
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:23,570
Something smells amazing.

10
00:00:24,270 --> 00:00:26,740
Is that beef stew?

11
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:27,780
Yeah.

12
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:29,400
No way!

13
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:31,530
I'm the biggest fan of beef stew

14
00:00:31,530 --> 00:00:33,370
in the entire world.

15
00:00:33,740 --> 00:00:35,370
Though I've never actually been abroad.

16
00:00:35,950 --> 00:00:37,410
So I've heard.

17
00:00:37,410 --> 00:00:38,960
Heard?

18
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:41,920
Huh? What's that supposed to mean?

19
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:43,130
Ahem.

20
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:48,090
This is delicious!

21
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:49,630
Really?

22
00:00:50,030 --> 00:00:51,840
It's the best in the world!

23
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:56,350
You're seriously amazing.

24
00:00:57,470 --> 00:00:58,930
Mmm...

25
00:00:58,930 --> 00:01:02,800
(He looks so cute
when he's eating...)

26
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:04,600
So good.

27
00:01:07,230 --> 00:01:08,030
Oh.

28
00:01:08,030 --> 00:01:09,740
Right, what was that about an audition?

29
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:12,240
Oh, for the autumn cultural festival play.

30
00:01:12,910 --> 00:01:13,910
Remember that play we read?

31
00:01:13,910 --> 00:01:15,780
Shakespeare's 'Twelfth Night'?

32
00:01:15,780 --> 00:01:16,910
We decided to do that one.

33
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:18,330
Oh, I see.

34
00:01:18,330 --> 00:01:19,620
Good luck with that.

35
00:01:19,620 --> 00:01:20,410
No, no, no.

36
00:01:20,410 --> 00:01:21,410
How many times do I have to say it?

37
00:01:21,410 --> 00:01:23,040
You're doing it too, Minato.

38
00:01:23,670 --> 00:01:26,250
Wait, but... I mean...

39
00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:28,050
Our school's festival play

40
00:01:28,050 --> 00:01:30,220
gets a lot of attention.

41
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:32,680
An alumnus who's a TV producer

42
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:34,010
is going to supervise it.

43
00:01:34,010 --> 00:01:36,260
Wow, that's amazing...

44
00:01:36,260 --> 00:01:38,430
For a production that big...

45
00:01:38,430 --> 00:01:40,980
- There's no way I can do it.
- What are you talking about?

46
00:01:40,980 --> 00:01:43,350
You can totally do it.

47
00:01:43,350 --> 00:01:45,060
But...

48
00:01:46,310 --> 00:01:47,820
(Why does he get so serious)

49
00:01:47,820 --> 00:01:49,530
(whenever acting comes up?)

50
00:01:49,530 --> 00:01:51,240
But I really can't...

51
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:53,700
Besides,

52
00:01:53,700 --> 00:01:55,700
Viola, the protagonist
of 'Twelfth Night,'

53
00:01:55,700 --> 00:01:58,240
- She's a very special character.
- Oh.

54
00:01:58,240 --> 00:02:00,910
What do you mean, 'Oh'?

55
00:02:00,910 --> 00:02:02,750
Didn't I tell you to practice?

56
00:02:02,750 --> 00:02:04,830
Huh?

57
00:02:04,830 --> 00:02:06,580
Do you really want me to play a woman?

58
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:09,090
I'm not joking.

59
00:02:09,090 --> 00:02:12,510
I already gave you
the script and lines, didn't I?

60
00:02:12,510 --> 00:02:15,680
I still have them, but...

61
00:02:19,810 --> 00:02:21,890
So you kept them.

62
00:02:21,890 --> 00:02:24,650
(Is he actually serious?)
